					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-macleod" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1922529); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1922529&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608196148" alt="Agent MacLeod" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1922529)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-macleod" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1922529); return false;" >Agent MacLeod</a></span> <span class="odate time_1434864328 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Jun 2015 05:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2321346">
									

<p>Only two qualms with this: a minor typo I don't even consider worth looking up again to point out, and the weapon the agent carries into the office at the end. To quote <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/echofourdelta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(515520); return false;">EchoFourDelta</a></span> in <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-1209460/foundation-equipment">this thread</a>,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Submachine guns haven't been offensively or defensively relevant since the invention of the intermediate rifle cartridge and its propagation, which began well over half a century ago. They fell into even greater irrelevance with the invention of practical personal armor. The only reason they're still in the popular consciousness is simply because a lot of real-world organizations are slow to adapt.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd say change it to a pistol, but even then, it's nitpicking that doesn't really affect my vote.</p>

							</div>

								
					
